LLVM's matrix intrinsic lowering on by default, as in Xcode 27.0's clang (B-170, docs/formats/build.md "Clang's
driver"): its -print-pipeline-passes runs lower-matrix-intrinsics<minimal> at -O0 and lower-matrix-intrinsics and an
early-cse after lower-constant-intrinsics at -O1 to -Oz, for every target, while the matrix types stay off
(-fenable-matrix). The extra early-cse changes what later passes see: moonlight's ConnectionTester.c at -Os keeps a
loop's address live out of it, so the loop vectorizer leaves the loop, and the object has no __literal16 and
__literal8, as Xcode's.
--- a/llvm/lib/Passes/PassBuilderPipelines.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Passes/PassBuilderPipelines.cpp
@@ -268,7 +268,7 @@
              "no inline hierarchy exists in the profile"));
 
 static cl::opt<bool>
-    EnableMatrix("enable-matrix", cl::init(false), cl::Hidden,
+    EnableMatrix("enable-matrix", cl::init(true), cl::Hidden,
                  cl::desc("Enable lowering of the matrix intrinsics"));
 
